  "definition_keys": [],
  "heading": null,
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{The Center is an Abelian Normal Subgroup}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Theorem:\ngiven:\n. G ::= (X, *, e) is \\group\n. Z is \\set\nwhere: Z = \\center:of{G}\nthen:\n. e \"in\"? Z\n. forAll: x, y \"in\" G\n  where:\n  . x \"in\"? Z\n  . y \"in\"? Z\n  then:\n  . x * y \"in\"? Z\n  . x * y = y * x\n. forAll: x \"in\" G\n  where: x \"in\"? Z\n  then: x.inv \"in\"? Z\n. forAll: g, z \"in\" G\n  where: z \"in\"? Z\n  then:\n  . exists: m \"in\" G\n    suchThat:\n    . m \"in\"? Z\n    . g * z = m * g\nDocumented:\n. called: \"The Center is an Abelian Normal Subgroup\"\n. description: \"The center contains the identity, is closed under products and\n                inverses, is internally commutative, and is invariant under\n                conjugation.\"\nId: \"636bc6b8-be24-41fe-9833-6bc18420ed97\"",
